<title>USA: ADR REPORT - French drug ADRs active.</title>
<headline>ADR REPORT - French drug ADRs active.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of French drug companies traded in the United States were active on Friday on merger speculation after Elf Aquitaine put its Sanofi drug unit in play.</p>
<p>Shares of Elf were were up 7/8 at 45-5/8 on the NYSE while shares Rhone-Poulenc , which has agreed to merge its animal health activities with those of Merck &amp; Co, was up 1-1/2 33-7/8 on the NYSE.</p>
<p>Shares of British Telecom were down 3/4 at 66 on the New York Stock Exchange.  </p>
<p>The British High Court on Friday ruled against British Telecom in a legal challenge over new powers for the Oftel watchdog body.</p>
</text>
